      "message": "Architectural comment: this Git tree-walk / `SKIP_DIFFSTAT` handling should live inside `DiffOperationsImpl` (via `DiffOptions`) rather than `FileInfoJsonImpl`.\n\n`FileInfoJsonImpl` (`com.google.gerrit.server.change`) is intended to be a thin DTO mapper over `DiffOperations` (`com.google.gerrit.server.patch`) without direct `GitRepositoryManager` / `RevWalk` / `TreeWalk` logic. Putting `computeFromTreeWalk` in `FileInfoJsonImpl` introduces a few issues:\n\n1. **Layering \u0026 duplicated `FileInfo` mapping**: `FileInfoJsonImpl` now opens the repo, walks trees, and duplicates the `FileInfo` construction logic from `asFileInfo()`.\n2. **Merge commits (`parentCount \u003e 1`) and `base !\u003d null` are bypassed**: Because `computeFromTreeWalk` manually checks `if (newCommit.getParentCount() \u003e 1)` and falls back to `getFileInfoMap()`, merge commits (which often have the largest file lists) silently ignore `SKIP_DIFFSTAT`. `DiffOperationsImpl#computeDiffParameters` (`BaseCommitUtil`) already resolves the base/auto-merge commit for all commit types.\n3. **Duplicate `RevWalk` on cache miss**: Opening a `RevWalk` in `FileInfoJsonImpl` and then calling `diffs.getModifiedFilesCached()` (`modifiedFilesCache.get()`) opens a second `Repository`/`RevWalk` inside `ModifiedFilesCacheImpl.Loader` on cache misses. `DiffOperationsImpl` already has `loadModifiedFilesWithoutCacheIfNecessary(...)` specifically to check `modifiedFilesCacheImpl.getIfPresent()` and load via `ModifiedFilesLoader` reusing the already-open `RevWalk`.\n\n**Suggested design:**\n- Add `skipDiffStat` (or `skipFileDiffs`) to `DiffOptions`.\n- In `DiffOperationsImpl`, after resolving `diffParams` (including auto-merge) and loading `modifiedFiles` via `loadModifiedFilesWithoutCacheIfNecessary`, if `diffOptions.skipDiffStat()` is true, populate lightweight `FileDiffOutput` entries (with `changeType`, `oldPath`, `newPath`, `oldMode`, `newMode`, `oldSha`, `newSha`, and empty edits) using the already-open `RevWalk` instead of querying `FileDiffCache` (or carry the `DiffEntry` mode/SHA fields from `GitModifiedFilesLoader#toModifiedFile`, since `DiffFormatter#scan` already reads them during the tree walk).\n- Then `FileInfoJsonImpl` doesn\u0027t need `GitRepositoryManager` or `computeFromTreeWalk` at all—it just passes `DiffOptions` to `diffs.listModifiedFilesAgainstParent` / `diffs.listModifiedFiles` and reuses `asFileInfo()`.",
